{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2024-11-27T09:26:58+00:00", "text": "is that something you have set up already, or does it need to be written from scratch?", "id": "m-engineering-2024-11-27-402"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2024-11-27T09:27:03+00:00", "text": "the cache key is the hash of the raw input row, full stop. cache_stats should report against those hashes and nothing fancier.", "id": "m-engineering-2024-11-27-403"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2024-11-27T09:27:23+00:00", "text": "and I want that contract to stay narrow. every time someone folds another thing into the fingerprint we end up with a key nobody can explain to a user asking why their rerun did what it did.", "id": "m-engineering-2024-11-27-404"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2024-11-27T09:27:43+00:00", "text": "the row is the unit the dataset is made of, so the row is the unit the cache is keyed on.", "id": "m-engineering-2024-11-27-405"}
