{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2024-12-05T18:00:21+00:00", "text": "this is the fingerprinting issue right here, the second segment changes file to file even though the prompt_func is identical:\n\n```\n[one.py] Curator Cache Fingerprint String: 296cb6f9ceed11ea_f863c1445ea56722_gpt-4o-mini_text_False\n[two.py] Curator Cache Fingerprint String: 296cb6f9ceed11ea_1f200c7acbf974e4_gpt-4o-mini_text_False\n```\n\nso basically the hash is including file path info when it serializes the lambda.", "id": "m-pipeline-2024-12-05-267"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2024-12-05T18:12:25+00:00", "text": "python's `inspect.getsource` on a lambda includes the source file path in some serialization paths, that's a known gotcha, https://docs.python.org/3/library/inspect.html#inspect.getsourcefile", "id": "m-pipeline-2024-12-05-268", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "💡"}]}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "konrad", "created_at": "2024-12-05T18:13:20+00:00", "text": "@Dario, source the PR 211 implementation is based on: https://git.world.local/tencent-ailab/persona-hub/blob/main/code/openai_synthesize.py, might help with the cost mapping comments.", "id": "m-code-review-2024-12-05-509"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "konrad", "created_at": "2024-12-05T18:13:45+00:00", "text": "Every release day I tell myself I am logging off by 5 and then here we are.", "id": "m-code-review-2024-12-05-510", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "😅"}, {"author": "dermot", "emoji": "😅"}]}
{"channel": "releases", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2024-12-05T18:20:29+00:00", "text": "@Emil any update on your end?", "id": "m-releases-2024-12-05-114"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "gideon", "created_at": "2024-12-05T18:27:25+00:00", "text": "I'll take the fix on that, stripping the file path from the serialization input before hashing is the right call, and it's mine to sort out in caching-and-resume.", "id": "m-pipeline-2024-12-05-269"}
