{"channel": "releases", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "\"v0.1.15 is out\" just went to the team. I also flagged in it that appending to the input dataset between restarts is a trap, I had 200 rows added to an 800-row set and the resumed job came back with 800 results for 1000 requests, reassembly slotted by index, and half the rows had somebody else's answer without any sign of it on inspection.", "id": "m-releases-2025-01-14-245"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:00:12+00:00", "text": "the main thing I wanted on record: there is exactly one function that decides whether a row is reused or sent, and every processor calls it, online, batch and the local vLLM one, so any change there is a breaking change to every persisted cache and has to be treated that way", "id": "m-code-review-2025-01-14-989"}
